{
  "name": "MAVILERA: 8086 Laboratory",
  "short_name": "MAVILERA",
  "description": "The Intel 8086: an assembler in the style of Intel's ASM-86 and an instruction-level simulator with segmented memory, the flags, the I/O ports and NMI and INTR inputs, checked against the SingleStepTests 8086 suite. The BIU and EU view steps each instruction through a teaching model, clock by clock with the bus interface unit filling the instruction queue, or with clock counts calibrated to recorded P80C86A-2 traces.",
